# Frontend Coding Standards

## API Fetching
- Always use the native fetch API
- Do not use axios or other HTTP client libraries
- Example in [src/lib](mdc:PPL-C5/src/lib) for API utility functions

## Components
- Use shadcn/ui components that are already set up in the project
- Reference the setup in [components.json](mdc:PPL-C5/components.json)
- Check existing components in [src/components](mdc:PPL-C5/src/components) for examples

## Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Organize classes based on categories:
  1. Layout (display, position)
  2. Spacing (margin, padding)
  3. Typography (font, text)
  4. Colors (bg, text colors)
- Reference the Tailwind config in [tailwind.config.ts](mdc:PPL-C5/tailwind.config.ts)

## Comments
- Write technical and professional comments
- Avoid emojis or slang
- Focus on explaining complex logic and why decisions were made, not what the code does
